# Day 5 — Networking Fundamentals, Wireshark & Connectivity Troubleshooting
## Objective
The objective of Day 5 was to develop practical networking and troubleshooting skills using the existing Blackwood IT Lab.
Rather than studying networking concepts only in theory, I used Windows and Linux networking tools, Wireshark packet captures, DNS queries, TCP connection testing, and a controlled firewall failure to observe how communication actually occurs between systems.

Topics included:
- IPv4 addressing and subnetting
- Local versus routed traffic
- Default gateways
- ARP and MAC address resolution
- DNS resolution
- TCP and UDP ports
- ICMP
- TCP connection establishment
- Wireshark packet analysis
- Linux firewall troubleshooting
- Layered network troubleshooting
