# 1. Inspecting Windows Network Configuration
On AC02:
```cmd
ipconfig /all
```
The active network configuration was identified as:
```text
IPv4 Address:    192.168.50.126
Subnet Mask:     255.255.255.0
Default Gateway: 192.168.50.1
DNS Server:      192.168.50.20
```
The subnet mask:
```text
255.255.255.0
```
is equivalent to:
```text
/24
```
A `/24` IPv4 network uses 24 bits for the network portion and 8 bits for host addresses.
For the Blackwood network:
```text
Network:          192.168.50.0
First usable:     192.168.50.1
Last usable:      192.168.50.254
Broadcast:        192.168.50.255
Usable addresses: 254
```
This means AC02 (`.126`) and WS01 (`.20`) are members of the same local subnet.
