# 5. DNS Resolution
AC02 uses WS01 as its DNS server:
```text
192.168.50.20
```
DNS resolution was tested with:
```cmd
nslookup ws01.blackwood.local
```
and:
```cmd
nslookup google.com
```
This reinforced that AC02 sends DNS requests to WS01 even when resolving public Internet names.
The basic process is:
```text
AC02
  ↓
DNS query
  ↓
WS01
  ↓
DNS resolution / forwarding
  ↓
DNS answer
  ↓
AC02
```
This also reinforced why Active Directory clients should use the appropriate AD DNS infrastructure rather than simply relying on a home router or public DNS resolver.
