# 6. Testing Individual TCP Services
Network connectivity to specific services was tested from AC02 using PowerShell.
DNS on WS01:
```powershell
Test-NetConnection 192.168.50.20 -Port 53
```
Result:
```text
TcpTestSucceeded : True
```
SMB on WS01:
```powershell
Test-NetConnection 192.168.50.20 -Port 445
```
Result:
```text
TcpTestSucceeded : True
```
SSH on UBV01:
```powershell
Test-NetConnection 192.168.50.219 -Port 22
```
Result:
```text
TcpTestSucceeded : True
```
This demonstrated an important distinction:
```text
ping
```
tests ICMP reachability, while:
```powershell
Test-NetConnection <address> -Port <port>
```
can determine whether a specific TCP service is reachable.
A successful ping does not prove that SSH, SMB, DNS, or another service is accessible.
