# 7. Verifying SSH from the Server Side
On UBV01:
```bash
sudo ss -tulpn
```
confirmed that SSH was listening on TCP port 22.
The firewall configuration was checked with:
```bash
sudo ufw status
```
The OpenSSH rule was enabled.
This provided three separate pieces of evidence:
```text
SSH process listening on :22       ✓
Firewall permits OpenSSH           ✓
Remote TCP/22 test succeeds        ✓
```
This distinction is useful because a service can be running locally while still being unreachable remotely due to firewall or network configuration.
