# 11. ICMP Packet Capture
Wireshark was configured with the display filter:
```text
icmp
```
Traffic was generated from OPS01:
```bash
ping -c 4 192.168.50.20
```
Eight ICMP packets were observed:
```text
4 Echo Requests
4 Echo Replies
```
The packet details showed protocol encapsulation including:
```text
Frame
└── Ethernet II
    └── Internet Protocol Version 4
        └── Internet Control Message Protocol
```
An Echo Request showed:
```text
Type: 8
```
and the corresponding Echo Reply showed:
```text
Type: 0
```
This demonstrated that `ping` uses ICMP rather than TCP or UDP.
Because ICMP is not TCP or UDP, ping does not test a service port.
